>> title: Ham Hock Stock, Instant Pot
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, stock, southern, smoked, instant pot, pressure cooker, make-ahead
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot ham hock stock, pressure cooker ham hock broth, instant pot pot likker, smoked pork stock, smoked pork pot, seasoning meat, smoked turkey stock
>> servings: 12
>> dish: ham-hock-stock
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: collard-greens, green-beans, black-eyed-peas, butter-beans
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — salt goes in at the end, because the hocks are already salty and a sealed pot concentrates further than an open one

>> step: rinse, into the pot with the aromatics
Rinse @smoked ham hocks{2}(about 2 lb / 900 g), @smoked pork neck bones{1%lb}(450 g) and lay them in the #Instant Pot{} with @cold water{2 1/2%qt}(2.4 L), @yellow onion{1%large}(halved), @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed), @bay leaves{2}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp} and @dried red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: cook at high pressure 45 min
Lock the lid on @&(~1)pot{} and ~pressure cook{45%min} at high pressure.

>> step: wait out the natural release 20 min
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops.

>> step: strain, pick the meat off the bone, salt at the end
Strain @&(~1)pot{} through a #fine sieve{} and pick the meat off the bone.
